WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.668
 Well, Chris, Damond,
congratulations.

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:04.137
You guys are moving forward
in the third and final round

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:05.638
of our competition.

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:07.173
Now, gentlemen, in
this last round,

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.474
we're going to be sending
you back to your home forges

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:10.175
to build one of
three iconic weapons

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:12.345
from our Fortune
Fire vault. We've

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:17.484
got the pandat, the
boa-zande, and the kelewang.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:22.321
Now, gentlemen, we've got
to keep to the casino theme,

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:25.392
so we're going to spin the
Wheel of Forging again.

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:28.061
But here's the deal-- if you
don't like where you land,

00:00:28.128 --> 00:00:30.963
you have an option to press
your luck and spin again.

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:34.834
But those 4 days
total the 35 hours.

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:37.737
If you choose to spin again,
we're going to be deducting

00:00:37.803 --> 00:00:39.572
2 hours from that total time.

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:43.676
Ready to find out what
you're building at home?

00:00:43.776 --> 00:00:44.777
- Let's do it.
- Let's do it.

00:00:44.877 --> 00:00:46.279
 Chris, you're up first.

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:47.180
 All right.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:54.087
 Oh-- all right.

00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:55.855
Chris, you landed on the pandat.

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:56.689
How are you feeling?

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:57.690
 I'll keep it.

00:00:57.790 --> 00:00:59.025 line:14%
I don't want to get that thing.

00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:00.460 line:14%
[laughter]

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:01.494
 Fair enough.

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:03.096
NARRATOR: The pandat
is a two-handed war

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:06.365
sword native to the Dayaks
of Borneo in Indonesia.

00:01:06.432 --> 00:01:08.802
Exclusively used in
combat, the weapon's

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:10.970
single-edged blade
was uniquely angled

00:01:11.036 --> 00:01:13.272
and featured a wide, flat tip.

00:01:13.372 --> 00:01:16.676
The ornate design made it a
very effective lethal weapon,

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:19.011
delivering devastating
chops through the armor

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:21.047
of an opponent.

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:23.115
This fierce sword was
featured in season three

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:25.918
of "Forged in Fire," where
the smiths both turned

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:27.419
in beautiful weapons.

00:01:27.486 --> 00:01:30.957
But ultimately, the better
balanced blade won the title.

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:32.058
 Damond, you ready?

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:33.093
Let's go.

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:41.100
The kelewang.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.236 line:8%
 So of course, I
get the kelewang.

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:45.571 line:8%
I don't have a quench tank that
would fit something like that.

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:48.107 line:8%
The odds of it landing
on kelewang again

00:01:48.207 --> 00:01:50.009 line:8%
are not too high, so
I'm willing to bet

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:51.944 line:14%
to get one of the other two.

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:53.045
Hit me again.
- All right.

00:01:53.112 --> 00:01:54.113
That means we're
going to be taking

00:01:54.213 --> 00:01:55.648
2 hours off your 35 hours.

00:01:55.714 --> 00:01:58.651
You will have 33 hours to
build whatever I land on.

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:04.858 line:14%
The boa-zande.

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:05.891 line:14%
You happy with it?

00:02:05.958 --> 00:02:07.493
 Oh, yeah.

00:02:07.593 --> 00:02:09.728
NARRATOR: The boa-zande sword
is a Central African weapon that

00:02:09.828 --> 00:02:13.899
features a long pierced ricasso
and a wide-leaf shaped blade

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.368
that tapers to a
steep, sharp tip.

00:02:16.435 --> 00:02:18.304
The razor-sharp
edges were designed

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:21.874
to deliver devastating stabs
and slashes into an enemy.

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:25.211
The boa-zande was previously
seen in season seven of "Forged

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:29.215
in Fire," where, while both
smiths faced challenges

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:31.084
achieving the width
of this weapon,

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:34.220
victory went to the lighter,
more comfortable sword.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.722
 All right, Chris,
you're going to have

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:37.523
35 hours to build your pandat.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.859
Damond, you've got 33 hours
to build your boa-zande.

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:43.095
And gentlemen, don't forget,
these are high stakes.

00:02:43.195 --> 00:02:45.198
The house is putting
up $10,000 in the title

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:46.932
of "Forged in Fire"
champion for the winner.

00:02:46.999 --> 00:02:47.933
Good luck.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:48.700
We'll see you in four days.

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:49.601
 Good luck, man.

00:02:49.668 --> 00:02:50.436 line:14%
 Good.

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:54.373 line:14%
 My name is Chris Gardner.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:58.310 line:8%
I am 37 years old,
from Las Vegas, Nevada.

00:02:58.377 --> 00:03:01.948
I'm doing a sword
with 327 layer billet.

00:03:02.014 --> 00:03:03.148
Looks like I have enough steel.

00:03:03.215 --> 00:03:04.884
I'm pretty happy
with how it's going.

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:06.652
It's looking pretty good so far.

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:08.655
Something goes wrong
with the quench,

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:12.158
I could basically
destroy my blade.

00:03:12.224 --> 00:03:15.861
Planning for the worst,
hoping for the best.

00:03:15.961 --> 00:03:17.897
All right, here we go.

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:21.067
I get it over to
the quench tank,

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:25.438
and it comes out straight.

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:26.505
That's good.

00:03:26.572 --> 00:03:27.306
Hard.

00:03:27.372 --> 00:03:28.874
This blade is a little awkward.

00:03:28.941 --> 00:03:33.012 line:8%
It's a weird shape I need a
specific edge on this thing

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:34.747 line:8%
that's going to hold
up during these tests

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:37.049 line:14%
and still stay sharp.

00:03:37.115 --> 00:03:38.684 line:14%
Damond, he's an excellent smith.

00:03:38.784 --> 00:03:41.087 line:8%
Can't wait to see what
he brings, but you know,

00:03:41.187 --> 00:03:43.423 line:8%
I hope mine's just
a little bit better.

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:49.695 line:14%
 My name is Damond Clark.

00:03:49.795 --> 00:03:51.430 line:14%
I am 45 years old.

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:54.267
Started doing Brazilian
Jujitsu about 12 years ago,

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:56.135
so I think that part of the
reason I'm a pretty decent

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:58.738
blacksmith is the
discipline and the strength

00:03:58.805 --> 00:04:00.239
it takes to be in jujitsu.

00:04:00.339 --> 00:04:01.708
It's looking good so far.

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:04.210
I'm going to draw out the
basic blade shape for now.

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:06.279
I gotta worry about
getting parameter lengths.

00:04:06.345 --> 00:04:07.613
We'll just see how things go.

00:04:07.713 --> 00:04:10.415
So 243 layers, that's
what I was shooting for.

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:11.784
I really like the
look of bronze,

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:14.553
so I'm going to put a
bronze guard and pommel.

00:04:14.653 --> 00:04:16.822
So I've got my pommel
tapped, and now I

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:19.058
need to thread my tank.

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:21.394
Shoot, I don't think
this is going to work.

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:23.395
I see that the
threads are not right.

00:04:23.462 --> 00:04:25.898
With the threads as
shallow as they are,

00:04:25.999 --> 00:04:27.233
it's not going to
grab the pommel,

00:04:27.299 --> 00:04:28.534
and it's not going to be tight.

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:31.137
I build the new pommel,
I get it on the handle.

00:04:31.204 --> 00:04:33.038
Everything looks
good, it's tight.

00:04:33.138 --> 00:04:34.607
That's going to work just fine.

00:04:34.673 --> 00:04:36.808
Now I'm ready to
start moving forward.

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:38.077
It looks great.

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:39.645
The pattern is really
showing really well.

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:41.380
So now it's time to get
the final edge on it,

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:43.482
and get this sucker sharp.

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:46.818
Losing two hours didn't really
change my plan of action.

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:48.021
She's a winner.

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:50.823
I feel really good
about what I made.

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:53.959
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to the kill test.

00:04:54.026 --> 00:04:56.896
I'm going to take your weapon
and deliver some lethal strikes

00:04:56.996 --> 00:04:58.597
on this big carcass.

00:04:58.698 --> 00:05:00.566
Because these are two
different kinds of weapons

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:03.235
with different designs,
they may cut differently

00:05:03.302 --> 00:05:04.537
or perform differently.

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:06.972
But overall, the feeling
and the way I wield them

00:05:07.039 --> 00:05:08.274
should be the same.

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:09.709
Chris, you're up first.
You ready for this?

00:05:09.776 --> 00:05:10.543
 Yeah, let's do it.

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:23.221
[slashing]

00:05:23.288 --> 00:05:25.458
[chuckling]

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:29.262
All right, Chris, let's
talk about your pandat here.

00:05:29.362 --> 00:05:30.830
When I picked it up,
it felt so light.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:33.099
A little forward heavy, but
that's what it's supposed

00:05:33.165 --> 00:05:34.400
to be, because it's a chopper.

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:36.636
Your handle
construction is smooth.

00:05:36.702 --> 00:05:38.471
I can fit both hands perfectly.

00:05:38.571 --> 00:05:39.972
There's no extra space.

00:05:40.072 --> 00:05:43.141
Overall, sir, with the function
of a chopper like this,

00:05:43.242 --> 00:05:44.743
it will kill.

00:05:44.810 --> 00:05:45.945
 Thank you.

00:05:46.045 --> 00:05:46.912
 Damond, you're up next.

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:47.713
You ready, sir?

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:50.583
 Yes, sir.

00:05:50.650 --> 00:06:00.192
[slashing]

00:06:00.259 --> 00:06:01.027
Yeah.

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:07.333
 All right, Damond, let's
talk about your boa-zande here.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:10.569
Your handle construction
fits my hand perfectly.

00:06:10.636 --> 00:06:14.173
I like the palm swell there,
because it locks my hand in.

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:15.875
Your edges are sharp.

00:06:15.975 --> 00:06:19.612
They cut deeply and thrust
nicely through this carcass.

00:06:19.678 --> 00:06:22.180
Overall sir, your boa-zande--

00:06:22.281 --> 00:06:23.148
it will kill.

00:06:23.215 --> 00:06:23.983
 Yeah!

00:06:27.419 --> 00:06:29.054
 Welcome to our strength test--

00:06:29.121 --> 00:06:31.924
the porcelain pot chop.

00:06:31.991 --> 00:06:34.159
It's going to be a lot of fun
to see what your blades do

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:35.828
to the pots, but
I'm more concerned

00:06:35.895 --> 00:06:38.330
about what the pots do to
your blades and their edges.

00:06:38.397 --> 00:06:39.298
And Chris, you're up first.

00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:40.065
You ready to go?

00:06:40.165 --> 00:06:41.233
 Yeah.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:42.034
 I'll take it.

00:06:42.101 --> 00:06:55.815
[music playing]

00:06:55.882 --> 00:06:56.915
Chris, you survived.

00:06:56.982 --> 00:06:58.084
Good job.

00:06:58.184 --> 00:06:59.785
You've got a little
bit of glinting,

00:06:59.852 --> 00:07:01.987
and you got a couple
of slight rolls,

00:07:02.054 --> 00:07:03.222
but they're very minimal.

00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:06.392
Everything's still
straight, sharp, sturdy.

00:07:06.459 --> 00:07:07.359
Good job.

00:07:07.426 --> 00:07:08.427
 Thank you.

00:07:08.527 --> 00:07:10.029
 Damond, you ready to go?

00:07:10.129 --> 00:07:11.230
 Can we just talk this out?

00:07:11.297 --> 00:07:11.997
 No.

00:07:12.064 --> 00:07:32.318
[music playing]

00:07:32.418 --> 00:07:33.352
Damond, you survived.

00:07:33.419 --> 00:07:34.854
Good job.

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:37.056
Some minor glinting, a
couple low rolls on the edge,

00:07:37.123 --> 00:07:40.159
but I mean, still, overall,
a very sharp blade.

00:07:40.259 --> 00:07:40.959
Nice job.

00:07:41.026 --> 00:07:41.794
 Thank you.

00:07:46.365 --> 00:07:47.667
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:07:47.767 --> 00:07:50.769
This is the sharpness
test, the vine slice.

00:07:50.836 --> 00:07:52.371
To find out how sharp
your weapons are,

00:07:52.438 --> 00:07:54.940
I'm going to take your weapon
and slash through these vines.

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:55.908
Chris, you're up first.

00:07:55.975 --> 00:07:56.442
You ready?

00:07:56.542 --> 00:07:57.242
 I'm ready.

00:07:57.342 --> 00:07:58.043
 All right.

00:07:58.110 --> 00:08:14.827
[music playing]

00:08:14.894 --> 00:08:17.697
All right, Chris, let's
talk about your pandat here.

00:08:17.797 --> 00:08:20.833
Your edges easily cut
through the vines, sir.

00:08:20.933 --> 00:08:23.301
Overall, your
pandat, it will cut.

00:08:23.368 --> 00:08:24.536
 Thank you.

00:08:24.603 --> 00:08:26.438
 All right, Damond,
the final gamble.

00:08:26.505 --> 00:08:27.272
Are you ready, sir?

00:08:27.339 --> 00:08:28.040
 Yes, sir.

00:08:28.107 --> 00:08:28.774
 Let's do this.

00:08:28.875 --> 00:08:44.023
[music playing]

00:08:44.089 --> 00:08:45.525
All right, Damond.

00:08:45.625 --> 00:08:48.594
The edges are sharp and cut
cleanly through the vines.

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:51.329
Your weapon, too,
sir, it will cut.

00:08:51.396 --> 00:08:53.432
 Thank you.

00:08:53.498 --> 00:08:55.734
 Well, well, well.

00:08:55.834 --> 00:08:59.438
Both of your weapons performed
extremely well in all three

00:08:59.505 --> 00:09:01.040
of our tests.

00:09:01.107 --> 00:09:03.409
But in this competition, we have
to have a winner, which means

00:09:03.509 --> 00:09:04.911
one of you has to go home.

00:09:05.011 --> 00:09:07.279
And the winner of today's
"Forged in Fire" competition

00:09:07.346 --> 00:09:09.948
is--

00:09:10.048 --> 00:09:10.482
Chris.

00:09:10.583 --> 00:09:12.084
Congratulations.

00:09:12.151 --> 00:09:14.520
Now, Damond, unfortunately, your
blade just didn't make the cut,

00:09:14.587 --> 00:09:16.088
and Jay is going
to tell you why.

00:09:16.188 --> 00:09:18.424
 Damond, you've got everything
in the world to be proud of.

00:09:18.491 --> 00:09:20.293
They tested equally.

00:09:20.359 --> 00:09:22.395
Fit and finish in
the finer details

00:09:22.495 --> 00:09:24.463
is what it came down to,
and Chris just squeaked

00:09:24.530 --> 00:09:25.330
a little bit ahead of you.

00:09:25.397 --> 00:09:26.198
That's it.

00:09:26.265 --> 00:09:27.700
 Cool.

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:29.901
 Damond, up against any other
blade, it would have won.

00:09:30.001 --> 00:09:32.705
But unfortunately, you did not
come out with the win today.

00:09:32.772 --> 00:09:33.872
I'm going to have
to ask you to please

00:09:33.972 --> 00:09:35.707
step off the Forged floor, man.

00:09:35.807 --> 00:09:36.942
 Thanks for having me, guys.

00:09:37.009 --> 00:09:38.810
Good job, buddy.

00:09:38.911 --> 00:09:40.846 line:8%
I know that with what they
told me about my weapon,

00:09:40.946 --> 00:09:43.449 line:8%
that there really
wasn't a loser here.

00:09:43.516 --> 00:09:46.118
I'm taking home just a
fantastic experience.

00:09:46.185 --> 00:09:48.387
This competition is amazing.

00:09:48.487 --> 00:09:50.055
I am humbled by this.

00:09:50.122 --> 00:09:52.090
It's been wonderful.

00:09:52.157 --> 00:09:54.393
 Chris, you are the
"Forged in Fire" champion,

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:57.395
and you're going to be taking
home a check for $10,000, man.

00:09:57.496 --> 00:09:58.263
Congratulations.

00:09:58.363 --> 00:09:59.598
 Aw, thank you, guys.

00:09:59.664 --> 00:10:00.599
Thank you so much.

00:10:00.699 --> 00:10:02.201
I'm, like, in disbelief.

00:10:02.267 --> 00:10:05.237
This title of "Forged in Fire"
champion means a lot to me.

00:10:05.304 --> 00:10:08.640
It's something that I
can always take with me.

00:10:08.741 --> 00:10:10.509
I am the "Forged
in Fire" champion!

00:10:10.576 --> 00:10:12.878
[music playing]

